course: dictionary
lesson: 10157
title: Thump: a hit, a sound, a beating heart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves» uses thump as a sound. The words around it, a heap of sticks and dry leaves, tell you it is a soft, dull noise, like a fall.
explain: «The Gryphon thumps the sobbing Mock Turtle» uses thump as an action. To thump means to hit something hard, usually with your fist. Hitting someone is never allowed, even when a story shows it.
explain: «Picture the last lap on sports day: face red, chest heaving, heart thumping in your ears.» Here your heart thumps because it is beating fast and hard. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Thump can be a verb (thump, thumps, thumped, thumping) or a noun (a thump, thumps).
fact: To thump means to hit something hard, usually with your fist, making a dull, heavy sound.
fact: A thump is a hit like that, or a heavy, dull sound, like something falling.
fact: «Heart thumping» means a heart beating fast and hard, often from effort or fear.
fact: «A rabbit thumps its back foot» to warn other rabbits of danger, and the thud travels through the ground.
exercise: «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves.» What is the thump here? | A sweet smell from the leaves | *A heavy, dull sound, like something falling | A happy song | A soft blanket
exercise: «His heart thumps, his cheeks go hot, and he shoves the tablet under a cushion.» What does heart thumps show? | His heart feels cold | *His heart is beating fast and hard | His heart is making music | His heart has stopped
exercise: «The Gryphon thumps the sobbing Mock Turtle.» Find and copy one word that means to hit something hard with your fist. | Gryphon | Turtle | sobbing | *thumps
test: «A rabbit thumps its back foot to warn other rabbits of danger.» Why does the rabbit thump? | To dig a new burrow | *To warn other rabbits of danger | To play a game | To go to sleep
test: «Picture the last lap on sports day: face red, chest heaving, heart thumping in your ears.» What does heart thumping mean? | Your heart is quiet and slow | *Your heart beats fast and hard | Your heart has gone cold | Your heart is full of sand
exam: Which phrase uses thump as a noun? | *land with a thump | thumps its back foot | to thump on the door | heart thumping
